    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0025",
      "sequence": 880,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa claims to be the mighty one whose arms made Kailāsa tremble, whose prowess Umāpati knows, and who repeatedly cut off his lotus heads with his own hands as offerings to Tripurāri. The guardians still feel his arm-strength and the elephants of the quarters know his chest’s hardness: their terrible tusks broke against it like radishes. When he walks, Earth sways like a small boat under a maddened elephant. He calls himself world-renowned and Aṅgada a tiny, barbarous liar who praises a mere man.",
